<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodora (wife of Justinian I)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 497–548</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodora was a Byzantine empress, wife of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> and one of the most influential women in Byzantine history. A former actress, she married Justinian around 525 and became empress in 527; during the Nika riots of 532 she is said to have persuaded him not to flee. She protected the Miaphysites, sponsoring missions such as the one that converted the Nubian kingdom of Nobadia around 543.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodora-wife-of-justinian-i.jpg" alt="Theodora (wife of Justinian I)" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petar Milošević · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theodora_mosaic_-_Basilica_San_Vitale_(Ravenna)_v2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
